  "description": "This race is for South Carolina's 2nd Congressional District, which covers Lexington County and portions of Richland, Aiken, Barnwell, and Orangeburg counties. Incumbent Republican Rep. Joe Wilson, first elected in 2001, is seeking re-election after winning the Republican primary with 74.2% of the vote. The Democratic primary advanced to a June 23 runoff between David Robinson II, a disabled wartime combat veteran, and Zyon Khalifa, with the winner becoming the Democratic nominee. Dayna Alane Smith of the Workers Party is also on the general election ballot. The district is rated as 'Solid Republican' by the Cook Political Report, making Wilson the heavy favorite in November.",
